# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles must always have LF line endings,
# regardless of the checking-out platform's core.autocrlf setting — a
# CRLF shebang line makes the kernel's exec() fail with a misleading
# "no such file or directory" the first time the container actually runs
# the script (discovered deploying from a Windows checkout: `git archive`
# honors the same line-ending conversion as checkout, so this bit even a
# clean `git archive <tag>` export, not just a working-tree copy).
*.sh text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
